<section class="page-intro shell">
  <p class="eyebrow">Product roadmap</p><h1>Where StylePort is headed.</h1>
  <div class="page-lede"><p>StylePort 1.0 is available as a signed direct download while the TestFlight beta continues. This roadmap shows what comes next for Apple distribution and the longer-term direction.</p></div>
</section>
<section class="roadmap shell" aria-label="StylePort product roadmap">
  <div class="roadmap-grid">
    <article class="roadmap-card roadmap-now">
      <div class="roadmap-meta"><span class="roadmap-status">Available now</span><span>Version 1.0</span></div>
      <h2>Direct Mac release</h2>
      <p>The complete Safari-first UserCSS experience is available as a Developer ID–signed and Apple-notarized direct download.</p>
      <ul><li>Plain CSS and UserCSS import from file, URL, or paste</li><li>Variables, compilation, and precise URL matching</li><li>Style editing, updates, export, and backup restore</li><li>Safari permission diagnostics and injection reliability</li><li>Signed Sparkle updates with user-approved installation</li><li>Corresponding GPL source and release verification files</li></ul>
    </article>
    <article class="roadmap-card roadmap-next">
      <div class="roadmap-meta"><span class="roadmap-status">Next</span><span>After 1.0</span></div>
      <h2>Mac App Store release</h2>
      <p>Continue TestFlight testing and prepare the Apple-distributed edition for App Review. The Mac App Store listing stays “Coming soon” until Apple’s public release is live.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="roadmap-card roadmap-later">
      <div class="roadmap-meta"><span class="roadmap-status">Later</span><span>Future release</span></div>
      <h2>iPhone and iPad</h2>
      <p>Explore an iOS and iPadOS container after the Mac experience and release process are reliable, adapting StylePort’s library and controls for smaller screens.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="roadmap-card roadmap-ongoing">
      <div class="roadmap-meta"><span class="roadmap-status">Ongoing</span><span>Every release</span></div>
      <h2>Safari compatibility and polish</h2>
      <p>Keep improving WebKit compatibility, accessibility, permission explanations, import reliability, and the everyday editing experience.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="roadmap-note">Plans can change as testing and Safari evolve. The roadmap describes direction, not a promised delivery date.</p>
</section>
